The resource obligation is moved to actual cleanup completion, not deleted.
A later lowering failure, missing closure, unsupported hook or omitted exit
must fail translation or keep an unproved/static-false result. Never replace
False with True, suppress assertions, or equate Finalizable with no leak.

Local fresh declarations:
    choose declaration + enclosing lexical continuation as a region
    use existing scoped variable and call-argument machinery
    attach actual Finalize before the original end-of-scope leak check
    use the same nested-initialization and exceptional-edge discipline
    preserve existing borrow restorations, finally blocks and CFG transfer
Do not duplicate finalization through both an existing finally section and
new scope cleanup. One owner/one retirement action on any realized exit path.

Region closure audit (compiler-state validation, not semantic proof):
    every deferred leak site belongs to exactly one exact-node region
    every region has all actual completion/raise/early-return exits covered
    no region begins before successful value initialization
    no owner is both transferred and finalized on the same path
    logical Old map remains complete and available through postchecks
Semantic validity of Finalize and absence of live referents are generated
proof obligations in addition to this structural audit.

Prohibited shortcuts:
    no blanket Finalizable exemption; no allocator call marked nonallocating
    no normal compiler/runtime expansion globally enabled in GNATprove mode
    no unproved new callee contracts, imported cleanup axiom or Assume
    no free of a copied source view; no default permission change for Adjust
    no missing source unit or incompatible historical-master implementation

